%% An unknown outcome and its resolution.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as Client thread
    participant H as Holder H
    participant O as Owner of term T
    participant V as Voters
    participant N as Next owner
    H->>V: replicate(T, root R) (something acceptable left, H7)
    V--xH: acknowledgements lost, late, or refused
    Note over H: permission validity ends without an observed majority (D46)<br/>(an owner that gets no done within valid + request_timeout acts as for unknown)
    H-->>T: ProtoOutcomeUnknownError (never retried by Database.run, D44 R35)
    H->>O: done(T, seq, inc, unknown)
    Note over O: rule O6: abandon the term, suspect T,<br/>refuse queued requests (abandoned), release with certain=False (D50)
    O->>V: release(T, certain=False)
    Note over V: suspect T: later grant replies are uncertain (D46)
    N->>V: request(T' > T)
    Note over V: promise T': no root of T accepted from now on (ballot rule)
    V-->>N: grant(accepted roots, certain=False)
    alt R reached a majority (it took effect)
        Note over N: the phase-1 value is R or above it (R127): R stays in the history
    else R was accepted by a minority, or by nobody
        Note over N: the base may or may not include R (R123):<br/>adopted when a granter reports it, dropped forever otherwise
    end
    Note over T: the application resolves by reading: an acknowledged id is present,<br/>an unknown one is present everywhere or absent everywhere (R86)
